WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.280 --> 00:00:09.670
The word ‘Cryptid’ refers to any entity
whose existence has yet to be documented outside

00:00:09.670 --> 00:00:12.990
of legends and myths — like… the loch
ness monster.

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:17.980
But believe it or not, many real animals you
might recognize today were once ‘cryptids’

00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:20.960
themselves, thought to exist only in folklore.

00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:26.460
As humankind has explored more and more remote
parts of our planet’s surface, increasingly

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:29.270
fantastical organisms have been discovered.

00:00:29.270 --> 00:00:34.820
So, for this entry into the archives, we’re
going to catalogue seven real animals once

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:37.809
upon a time thought to be cryptids.

00:00:37.809 --> 00:00:41.359
In the darkness of the ocean, a leviathan
lurks.

00:00:41.359 --> 00:00:47.420
For centuries, sailors made reports of a colossal,
tentacled monster which emerged from the depths

00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:50.800
to drag ships to their watery demise.

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:56.359
Referred to in Scandinavian folklore as the
Kraken, for most of human history, these supposed

00:00:56.359 --> 00:00:59.769
sea monsters were thought to be nothing more
than a myth.

00:00:59.769 --> 00:01:06.880
Today, however, scientists believe these tales
emerged from early sightings of giant squids.

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:12.570
Since the first footage of a live adult giant
squid wasn’t captured until the 2000s, it’s

00:01:12.570 --> 00:01:17.360
no surprise these creatures were considered
to be fictitious monsters for so long.

00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:23.200
They don’t actually smash boats, but since
these cephalopods can grow up to 13 meters

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:29.219
or 43 feet in length, it’s not shocking
these behemoths were once considered true

00:01:29.219 --> 00:01:34.940
monsters Additionally, the animals have the
largest eyes of any living creature, about

00:01:34.940 --> 00:01:36.539
the size of a dinner plate.

00:01:36.539 --> 00:01:40.479
They also have three hearts and a donut-shaped
brain that their esophagus passes through

00:01:40.479 --> 00:01:42.909
the middle of on the way to their stomach.

00:01:42.909 --> 00:01:49.009
In a way, it would almost make more sense
if giant squids were only the stuff of legends.

00:01:49.009 --> 00:01:55.119
Besides the Kraken, one of the most recognizable
aquatic cryptids is the sea serpent.

00:01:55.119 --> 00:02:01.159
Taking on various different forms in numerous
cultures, sea serpents are usually long, scaly

00:02:01.159 --> 00:02:05.039
monsters, sometimes sporting a finned ridge
going down their backs.

00:02:05.039 --> 00:02:10.039
Although such a monster seems like it could
only exist in myth, there is one real species

00:02:10.039 --> 00:02:14.900
which scientists consider to be a probable
source of many sea serpent tales.

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:20.260
The Oarfish (or-fish) is a massive deep-sea
organism which swims at such a low depth it’s

00:02:20.260 --> 00:02:22.459
challenging to capture footage of one.

00:02:22.459 --> 00:02:29.379
While a fish, not a serpent, the oarfish can
reach lengths of 8 meters, or 26 feet in length.

00:02:29.379 --> 00:02:34.599
During storms, these giants sometimes washed
up on the shore, which is likely where ancient

00:02:34.599 --> 00:02:36.560
humans first encountered them.

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:41.599
In some rare cases, however, the oarfish has
been spotted swimming in shallow tropical

00:02:41.599 --> 00:02:48.069
waters, a sight which is the closest you’ll
ever get to observing a ‘real sea serpent.’

00:02:48.069 --> 00:02:53.160
Moving onto land, another large reptilian
cryptid that appears in the folklore of many

00:02:53.160 --> 00:02:55.310
cultures is the dragon.

00:02:55.310 --> 00:03:00.090
Four limbed, fire breathing monsters with
a serpentine appearance, true dragons might

00:03:00.090 --> 00:03:05.610
only exist in old tomes, but there’s a real-world
animal that gets pretty close.

00:03:05.610 --> 00:03:10.849
Komodo Dragons aren’t the origin of most
dragon myths, but when they were first reported

00:03:10.849 --> 00:03:16.160
on, it’s no surprise people were at first
skeptical of accounts of massive, scaly beasts

00:03:16.160 --> 00:03:18.880
which seemed right out of ancient legend.

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:24.599
Growing up to a length of 3 meters, or 10
feet, the largest lizards on the planet aren’t

00:03:24.599 --> 00:03:27.030
that far off from actual dragons.

00:03:27.030 --> 00:03:31.930
They might not breathe fire, but they do produce
toxic proteins from glands in their lower

00:03:31.930 --> 00:03:32.930
jaw.

00:03:32.930 --> 00:03:35.299
Not an animal you want to mess with.

00:03:35.299 --> 00:03:39.930
Returning to the open waters, krakens and
sea serpents weren’t the only fantastic

00:03:39.930 --> 00:03:42.379
creatures sailors told tales of.

00:03:42.379 --> 00:03:46.909
Many also made references to mermaids, the
fish tailed sirens of the deep.

00:03:46.909 --> 00:03:52.430
But these sightings were in fact inspired
by glimpses of a real animal.

00:03:52.430 --> 00:03:53.569
The manatee.

00:03:53.569 --> 00:03:58.840
Manatees are herbivorous marine mammals which
look decidedly not like people, although they

00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:04.290
feature unique paddle-shaped tails which do
tangentially resemble mermaids of legends.

00:04:04.290 --> 00:04:08.959
The sailors who spotted these creatures likely
only saw them from a distance, and had maybe

00:04:08.959 --> 00:04:11.719
spent too much time alone on their boats.

00:04:11.719 --> 00:04:16.070
Mermaids or not, Manatees are great, play
a vital role in their ecosystem, and must

00:04:16.070 --> 00:04:17.870
be protected.

00:04:17.870 --> 00:04:22.180
Moving inland, I want you to imagine a dense
forest.

00:04:22.180 --> 00:04:27.310
Now imagine a large, furry, unknown animal
which sometimes can be spotted walking on

00:04:27.310 --> 00:04:29.280
two legs like a human.

00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:33.460
If your mind first went to bigfoot, I’d
understand — but these are actually the

00:04:33.460 --> 00:04:38.690
details of a completely different primate
species that once was unknown to science:

00:04:38.690 --> 00:04:40.210
the mountain gorilla.

00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:41.210
Crazy, right?

00:04:41.210 --> 00:04:46.520
Today, the existence of gorillas seems obvious,
but if you try to imagine getting a report

00:04:46.520 --> 00:04:51.551
of gigantic, hairy upright-walking animals
hiding in heavily forested mountains, you

00:04:51.551 --> 00:04:56.870
might start to sympathize more with any initial
doubters of these creatures’ existence.

00:04:56.870 --> 00:05:01.560
Some early accounts suggested they were violent
carnivores, and although they’re no pushovers,

00:05:01.560 --> 00:05:05.509
they’re much more likely to munch on a carrot
than munch on a passerby.

00:05:05.509 --> 00:05:10.430
Like the Manatees, Gorillas are an amazing,
yet endangered species which needs to be safeguarded

00:05:10.430 --> 00:05:13.710
— or they might pass into myth.

00:05:13.710 --> 00:05:18.360
Down in the continent of Australia, we have
some of the most unique animals on earth.

00:05:18.360 --> 00:05:23.220
But perhaps none is quite so strange as a
certain duck-billed egg laying mammal which

00:05:23.220 --> 00:05:26.960
was for years thought to be just a mythical
cryptid.

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:29.750
I’m of course talking about the platypus.

00:05:29.750 --> 00:05:35.300
Unlike other species on this list, nobody
mistook the platypus for some existing mythical

00:05:35.300 --> 00:05:39.729
monster, because, frankly even things out
of myth don’t look as weird as the platypus.

00:05:39.729 --> 00:05:47.259
Instead, for years, many simply believed the
animal was a hoax.

00:05:47.259 --> 00:05:50.090
What an incredible species.

00:05:50.090 --> 00:05:54.650
And to close off our list, we have not an
animal, but a plant.

00:05:54.650 --> 00:05:58.919
Early records of Venus fly-traps were met
with skepticism, and considering they’re

00:05:58.919 --> 00:06:03.449
a plant which essentially — eat insects
within their mouth-like leaves, once can understand

00:06:03.449 --> 00:06:04.449
why.

00:06:04.449 --> 00:06:10.139
The idea of hordes of snapping plants which
catch live prey does sound pretty far-fetched,

00:06:10.139 --> 00:06:11.650
and pretty horrifying.

00:06:11.650 --> 00:06:16.729
The way Venus fly traps work is they possess
tiny hair like triggers which go off when

00:06:16.729 --> 00:06:20.740
insects land on them, releasing a signal to
trap them inside.

00:06:20.740 --> 00:06:25.289
The plants then digest the bugs using a unique
set of enzymes.

00:06:25.289 --> 00:06:31.810
And honestly, if that isn’t the closest
thing to a documented cryptid, I don’t know

00:06:31.810 --> 00:06:32.810
what is.

00:06:32.810 --> 00:06:38.280
So those are 7 animals—well, 6 animals and
one plant—that are no longer the stuff of

00:06:38.280 --> 00:06:39.280
myth.

00:06:39.280 --> 00:06:43.590
